#: ../../using/iscsi.rst:2 61d806c546ef48a080aab5c25d61dd36
msgid "Exporting a library over iSCSI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/iscsi.rst:4 7bafd346cf4d48b58e3ec82ea75c2235
msgid ""
"Exporting makes a library visible to another machine, which then sees a "
"tape library on its own SCSI bus and backs up to it as if it were plugged"
" in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/iscsi.rst:12 966be65ad61f45b6b99aabe6022553f2
msgid "What gets exported"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/iscsi.rst:14 cd5289be9982438e9a4fa710bd8196e8
msgid ""
"Three devices per library, at least: the robot, and each drive. Backup "
"software needs all of them - the robot to move cartridges, the drives to "
"write."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/iscsi.rst:23 5f83ed72688b467aab6992a95ffc3ea2
msgid ""
"That is library 50, which has two drives: one changer and two drives make"
" three LUNs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/iscsi.rst:26 05f521c9f94a4e0ca49d5b2c5c9f4305
msgid ""
"In the console it is **iSCSI → Export Library**, or **The library → "
"Export over iSCSI** on the library page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/iscsi.rst:29 b1e3c5a0ba4f43f9948a18b4da0f5f78
msgid "The iSCSI page, showing two exported libraries and their backstores"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/iscsi.rst:34 a8e212ad544c44deaad1cbd81c402ba7
msgid "What it made"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/iscsi.rst:53 1c8cc2e2118247399d5169db5f586dad
msgid "**IQN** is the target's name, which the other machine uses to find it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/iscsi.rst:55 76fd8f14227d4804a8f4aae5700b2467
msgid "The targets page: each export and what it holds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/iscsi.rst:59 e38309d05460469a9c8359bb79408094
msgid ""
"**ANY INITIATOR** means no access list: anything that can reach the port "
"may use it. To restrict it, export with ``--initiator``, or add an ACL:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/iscsi.rst:67 e2259cb370d648429b802ecab81db684
msgid "Connecting from another machine"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/iscsi.rst:69 9fccc3b32db143408960948aa1d304c9
msgid "On the client, with ``iscsi-initiator-utils`` installed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/iscsi.rst:83 836eb40579f3452f85e95baa94d1954a
msgid ""
"From there it is an ordinary tape library: ``mtx`` drives the robot, "
"``mt`` and ``tar`` the drives. The tutorial *Exporting a library with "
"Linux tools* in the *Guides* walks through a full backup and restore "
"across the wire."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/iscsi.rst:88 237b102c5a72458282159c7384520136
msgid "After a reboot, or after recreating a library"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/iscsi.rst:90 0ff5c45527394069952395bf18fbb7c4
msgid ""
"An export names devices by their ``/dev/sg`` node, and those numbers are "
"not stable: they change when the MHVTL module reloads, and when a library"
" is recreated. An export pointing at the wrong node is worse than one "
"that is missing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/iscsi.rst:95 cf0509dc37c243018d3ccf35d28b4d69
msgid ""
"The console keeps a record of which daemon each backstore was made for, "
"and repoints them by SCSI address:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/iscsi.rst:108 4d1483524abe4e85bbd393202f14a505
msgid ""
"The iSCSI page shows the same thing per device: **Created on** is the "
"node the backstore was made with, **Device now** is where that daemon "
"actually is, and **State** is ``BOUND`` when they agree. A stale one says"
" so."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/iscsi.rst:112 d25c6f2e4aea426ca75daee31231d108
msgid "This runs automatically at boot, through ``mhvtl-iscsi-remap.service``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/iscsi.rst:115 e60bea3ec6924c56bbaea2d5615c6f6b
msgid "Removing an export"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/iscsi.rst:122 1389b20ba43a426eb0779befaf1b8179
msgid "Log the client out first, or it keeps a session to a target that has gone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/iscsi.rst:124 4005f4eeb59c4bac839d2374a7c66acf
msgid ""
"The target goes; its **backstores stay**. They are the devices, and "
"deleting a target does not assume you meant to stop exporting them - the "
"same devices can be mapped into another target. ``mhvtl iscsi "
"backstores`` still lists them afterwards, and they are removed with "
"targetcli:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/iscsi.rst:137 f2c83b182ae44c9ab3e31356ad005d3e
msgid "Is the service even running?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/iscsi.rst:151 874bfac02bc442a99b1057539fd53e3f
msgid ""
"``config saved`` matters: LIO keeps its configuration in "
"``/etc/target/saveconfig.json``, and an export that was never saved is "
"gone at the next reboot. The console saves after every change."
msgstr ""

